  caseFiles:
  - title: Case Notes
    body: "\u2022 Trusted domain (case files): examplebank.example"
  - title: How This Room Works
    body: '1. 6 questions arrive one at a time, in a new order each attempt.


      2.
      Case questions: pick the safest, most accurate answer (A-D).


      3. Messages
      and web pages: choose SCAM or LEGITIMATE.


      4. Not sure? Press HINT to
      see what to look at. After each answer you''ll see why it was right or wrong.


      Goal:
      score 590+ to unlock the next room.'
  firstMessageDelay: 10
  delayBetweenMessages: {x: 10, y: 20}
  minimumActivityDelay: 5
  scoring:
    basePoints: 200
    speedBonus: 20
    fastWindow: 0.35
    wrongPenalty: 25
    recoveryPoints: 50
    baseReadingSeconds: 20
    secondsPerWord: 0.5
    secondsPerDetail: 3
    minReadingSeconds: 45
    maxReadingSeconds: 140
    caseExtraSeconds: 60
    overtimeStepSeconds: 10
    overtimePenaltyPerStep: 5
    maxTimePenalty: 25
    minCorrectPoints: 160
  oneStarScore: 405
  twoStarScore: 590
  threeStarScore: 1200
  minScoreToUnlockNext: 590
  nextLevelId: level_4
  nextSceneName: Room4_DigitalForensicsLab
  lessons:
  - Know that a padlock doesn't mean a site is real.
  - Spot scams that use feelings and rush you, and check through a number you know.
  - Report a security mistake quickly and honestly.
  - Pick the protection that fits the problem.
  - Spot fake Wi-Fi hotspots, and know what a VPN can't do.
  - Know that the name on your phone doesn't prove who sent a text.
  learningSummary: 
  performanceHigh: Outstanding analysis! You weighed every clue against the evidence
    and made sharp decisions.
  performanceModerate: Solid investigation. Review the explanations - the subtle
    cases reward checking the case files.
  performanceLow: Keep practising. Compare each sender and request with the case
